  "notes": "{微分|びぶん} is the mathematical operation of differentiation — finding the rate of change of a function. Compound of {微|び} (minute/slight) + {分|ぶん} (division).\n\nUSAGE:\nUsed as a する verb: {微分|びぶん}する (to differentiate).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {微分|びぶん}する: to differentiate\n- {微分|びぶん}{積分|せきぶん}: differential and integral calculus (often paired together)\n- {微分|びぶん}{方程式|ほうていしき}: differential equation\n- {偏|へん}{微分|びぶん}: partial differentiation\n- {微分|びぶん}{係数|けいすう}: derivative (coefficient)\n\nRELATED TERMS:\n- {積分|せきぶん}: integration (the inverse operation)\n- {導関数|どうかんすう}: derivative function\n- {関数|かんすう}: function\n\nEDUCATION:\nIn Japan, {微分|びぶん}{積分|せきぶん} (calculus) is typically introduced in the third year of {高校|こうこう} (high school) as part of the mathematics curriculum.",
